Current guide:

Convert:
	Action On Item Use (or whatever kit does for repairs, conditioned by having netherbrick and sword, and kit has kitType: 0b) ->
	Set variables for tier and durability:
		Set ivy.const to the sword's damage tag
		Set ivy.tmp to the SWORD's max durability based on tier
		Operation @s ivy.tmp -= @s ivy.const
		Operation @s ivy.tmp /= #2 ivy.const
		set ivy.const to correct tier.
		(MAY NEED TO CREATE NEW VARIABLES TO JUGGLE THESE, OR SET TIER IN SEPARATE COMMAND)
	Remove kit and Sword (action to delete the items in the player's hands)
	Call creation
	
Creation:
	Entirely in MC functions ->
	Get the data from scoreboard/resource/whatever, store it in storage
	summon nether brick. Depending on tier, name becomes "<tier> Armblade"
	Write tier into NBT tag
	Write durability into nbt tag.
	Write durability into lore. Format: "<durability>/<tier max>"
	OPTIONAL: write durability bar in 20ths of a percentage like before? Likely leave this out if there's no way to do it cleanly
	
Repair:
	Action On Block Use (conditioned by netherbrick in one hand where kitType > 0b, other hand is repair item matching tier, block is anvil)
	Set variables for tier and durability. Add 25% durability. Cap at max durability.
	Remove items
	Call creation
	
Uninstall:
	Action On Item Use (or whatever Kit's origin used for repairs, conditioned by netherbrick with kitType 0b, other hand NOT sword, and the installed tier resource is not 0) ->
	Write from resources into scoreboard, or copy into creation resources
	Delete empty kit
	call creation
	
Install:
	Action On Item Use (again, actually whatever Kit used. I want all of these abilities (except repair) require the player to hold right click for a bit. Conditioned by having kit in hand with type > 0b.) ->
	Write tier from item into installed resource. Do so in origins if possible, and if it doesn't require huge if-else chain.
	Delete item
	